                <pb facs="0945" n="933" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg933"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">703.5492/23: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-06-24">June 24, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1635. American interests—Thailand. Your 2712, June 14. Department perceives no
                    reason why copy of inventory should be transmitted to Thai Government.
                    Switzerland having undertaken protection <pb facs="0946" n="934" xml:id="pg934"
                    /> of this Government’s interests and property in Thailand, the Swiss
                    representative at Bangkok is proper repository of inventory.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
